    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_adcc4ebd",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: you-just-ran-past-full-retard-and-went-straight-to-potato; hasOverallIntent: Abusive; overall-intent-description: The image features a man with a stern, intense expression, overlaid with text that reads 'you just ran past full retard and went straight to potato.' The phrase 'full retard' is a derogatory slur targeting individuals with intellectual disabilities, falling under the category of ableism. The juxtaposition of the man's serious demeanor with the crude, insulting text creates a meme intended to mock or insult someone who allegedly failed to recognize or acknowledge a person with a disability. The use of such a slur is abusive and degrading, aiming to demean the target of the meme by invoking a harmful stereotype. The 'potato' reference is a common internet trope used to imply someone is unintelligent or foolish, further reinforcing the insult. The overall intent is to deliver a hostile, mocking message that targets individuals with disabilities, making it abusive in nature.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_bb555296"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
